{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1410,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are a lot of reasons for wanting a lava\nmoat around your house, but not that many"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5700,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how-to videos explaining how to build one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8880,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we’re here to change that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10370,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s actually pretty easy to make lava,\nat least in principle - the ingredients are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14610,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just rocks and heat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16510,
    "dDurationMs": 1029,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lots of heat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17539,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most rocks melt at temperatures between 800\nand 1200 celsius, which is hotter than your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22199,
    "dDurationMs": 4611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "oven, so you’ll need a gas or charcoal powered\nforge, or an electric furnace."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26810,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s tempting to choose a kind of rock or\neven metal or glass that melts at a lower"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31350,
    "dDurationMs": 4229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "temperature, but then it won’t glow as much:\nthe intensity and color of the glow depends"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35579,
    "dDurationMs": 4041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on how hot the lava is, and you definitely\nwant a lava moat that glows (preferably a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39620,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nice bright orange-yellow color)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41180,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For this reason, we recommend only top quality\nKeweenawan basalt obtained from the upper"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45780,
    "dDurationMs": 1610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "midwest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47390,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the challenges in maintaining a glowing\nlava moat is that it’s literally radiating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51270,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "away its energy in the form of heat and light;\nthis means you can’t simply melt your lava,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55300,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pour it into your moat, and call it a day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57260,
    "dDurationMs": 3799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your lava moat is going to need some kind\nof built-in heating apparatus to make up for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61059,
    "dDurationMs": 5271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the losses: a ceramic crucible with high temperature\nelectric heating coils will work just fine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66330,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you’ll definitely want a good layer\nof insulation to keep heat from leaking into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69050,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ground - because you’re going to need\na lot of heat!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71830,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the temperatures we’re working with,\nlava radiates roughly 100 kilowatts of heat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76410,
    "dDurationMs": 5110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "per square meter (that’s equivalent to 1000\n100-watt lightbulbs per square meter - though"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81520,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can’t fit 1000 100-watt light bulbs\ninto a square meter, if that gives you any"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85640,
    "dDurationMs": 2110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sense of how intense lava is)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87750,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anyway, electricity typically costs around\n10 cents per kilowatt hour, so each square"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92470,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meter of lava moat is going to cost you around\n$10 per hour."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96080,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means that a lava moat a meter wide and\nenclosing an area roughly the size of a football"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100110,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "field will cost $60,000 per day to keep running."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103030,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you don’t like the idea of being reliant\non somebody else to keep your lava moat home"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106830,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "security system operational, you could instead\npower it with solar panels, or build your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111040,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "own power plant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112210,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each of these has its pros and cons: solar\npower never needs fuel resupply shipments:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116200,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sun is going to keep burning for a while."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118530,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, every square meter of lava moat requires\n2000 square meters of solar panels to keep"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123390,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it glowing day and night."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125040,
    "dDurationMs": 3839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We don’t need to explain the security risks\nof putting your lava moat’s power source"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128879,
    "dDurationMs": 4371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outside of the protection of the lava moat,\nso if you want a lava moat a meter wide powered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133250,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entirely by solar panels inside of the moat,\nthe math works out that the moat needs to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137420,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "surround an array of solar panels 8 kilometers\nacross."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140810,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is clearly absurd."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142340,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can have a wider and yet more reasonable-sized\nmoat if you instead build your own commercial"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147250,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scale power plant inside it - coal and nuclear\npower plants produce enough energy to heat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151780,
    "dDurationMs": 4670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lava moat 10 meters wide and encircling\nan area 500 meters across - enough space to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156450,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fit the power plant and your house inside!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159120,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The downside is that (unless you build your\nmoat on top of a coal or uranium deposit)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163470,
    "dDurationMs": 5190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you’ll need to bring in outside fuel, so\nyour lava moat won’t be entirely off-grid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168660,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps the best off-grid option for powering\nyour lava moat is simply to take inspiration"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172740,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the source of lava itself: the earth’s\nown internal heat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176340,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Assuming you don’t have access to an island\nin a lava lake in an active volcano, the next"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180240,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "best option is geothermal power: by choosing\nthe right location, a good geothermal power"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185130,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plant can heat a modest-sized lava moat that’s\nperfect for protecting a single family home."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190930,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I suppose you might also want to learn about\nprecisely how wide your lava moat should be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195280,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to deter intruders, or how to cool your house\nonce it’s successfully encircled by lava,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199580,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or how to deal with all the noxious fumes\ngiven off by lava."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202200,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for that, you need to check out the full\nlava moat instructions available in the book,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205950,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "“How To” by Randall Munroe, which this\nvideo is based on (and supported by)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210080,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How To is an absurd and entertaining self-help\nguide full of ridiculous over-the-top advice"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214520,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about everything from how to dig a hole, to\nhow to be on time, to how to ski, to how to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219410,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "catch a drone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220410,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can find a how-to guide for how to obtain\na copy of “How To” in the video description,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224740,
    "dDurationMs": 5050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a big thanks to Randall and “How To”\nfor supporting and inspiring this “How To”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229790,
    "dDurationMs": 460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "video."
    } ]
  } ]
}
